SSH is enabled at boot by this port (etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/
sshd.socket), which stock Sailfish leaves disabled until you turn on Remote
connection in Developer tools.

Why: on a fresh install the developer page shows no connection address at all
until sshd is running, which reads as "Wi-Fi debugging is broken" when in fact
nothing is listening. For a port that people will need to debug remotely, having
it up from first boot is more useful than the stock default.

Consequence worth knowing: an SSH server listens on every interface the phone
has an address on, and it accepts the account password. Set a real one under
Settings -> Developer tools, or disable the service:

    systemctl disable --now sshd.socket
